Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:22:12.74,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,{\fs16\fnComic Sans MS}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.45,0:00:19.55,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Guarded by the Belafons, masters of fearsome magic, \Nthe sacred spring of the Dofus remains unsullied to this day.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.50,0:02:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H404040&\pos(42.667,251.022)}{\fs22}{\fad(700,1000)}{\4c&H000000&\4a&HFF&}Episode 4                                       
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.50,0:02:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H404040&\fs22\pos(140.8,249.6)}{\fad(700,1000)\4c&H000000&\4a&HFF&}Caramelized Skewers
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.03,0:02:40.83,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,An egg?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.35,0:02:46.73,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Or tea... \NIt seems they enjoyed a nice, slow meal here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.26,0:02:55.22,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,How does it look, Shifo? \NAny clues?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.70,0:03:00.94,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,My Prince, it appears they spent the night here. \NAnd their numbers have grown.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.58,0:03:05.14,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Allies? This might have been their hideout.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.88,0:03:08.52,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,There's a strong smell of sweat.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.20,0:03:14.16,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Prince, besides your cousin, \Nthere seem to be several others.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.60,0:03:17.76,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,And... a cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.76,0:03:23.24,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Indeed. Mother has enemies everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.89,0:03:31.56,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,The embers are still warm. \NThey haven't gone far.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.61,0:03:35.91,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,We likely missed them by mere moments.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.85,0:03:38.84,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,They must have left in a great hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.10,0:03:55.06,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I smell my father's poison. \NIt should have spread throughout his entire body by now.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.37,0:03:59.24,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Perhaps he is no longer among the living.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.37,0:04:03.76,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Either way, they have no hope of escaping.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.37,0:04:09.72,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Take me to him. \NI want to bring proof of his death to Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.36,0:04:23.00,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Mama, could you take the gratin out of the oven?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.04,0:04:27.44,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Now I just need to chop \Nthe carrots and peel the onions...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.44,0:04:31.24,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Ugh, the onions are stinging my eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.04,0:04:37.92,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Hey, the weather is nice today, \Nso let's make Mama's favorite meat skewers outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.08,0:04:49.80,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Dad! 
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.00,0:04:52.40,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,It's okay, don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.60,0:04:55.76,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,"Don't worry"? \NHow can I not worry?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.28,0:05:06.77,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Alright, I'll prepare the marinade then.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.22,0:05:14.58,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Mix the mustard with minced garlic...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.50,0:05:17.98,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Pour in olive oil...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.22,0:05:23.46,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Add honey for sweetness, \Nand lemon for acidity.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.74,0:05:25.50,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Are you using Bechamel's honey?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.22,0:05:30.26,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Of course! \NBechamel's honey is the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.73,0:05:43.26,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Don't forget to add herbs. \NRosemary would be great!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.13,0:06:02.30,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,The ratio of ingredients is crucial... \NMy favorite is...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.40,0:06:06.53,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,He's cooking... \NWelsh is fighting in his own way, isn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.74,0:06:13.86,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,My little friend, \Nit seems this boy is confusing fantasy with reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.62,0:06:21.34,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I hate myself for being so foolish... \NI didn't even notice I was poisoned by Azalar.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.10,0:06:26.62,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Nobody noticed. \NStop dwelling on pointless regrets \Nand focus on what's important now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.18,0:06:34.01,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I never thought things would turn out like this... \NWhat should I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.62,0:06:40.18,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,There's an order to things. \NFirst, we need to get this boy to a healer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.83,0:06:45.50,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Can this healer really cleanse dragon poison? \NThis is Azalar's poison! 
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.60,0:06:46.35,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Master Joris!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.07,0:06:50.41,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Welsh is alive because you saved him in Breshka!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.27,0:06:54.57,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,We know you are doing everything you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.55,0:06:58.19,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Please, don't give up now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.55,0:07:03.43,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Little one, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.51,0:07:08.01,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Ah, little one right! \NPlaying the tragic hero doesn't suit an old man like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.47,0:07:11.06,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Dad's healer is an amazing person!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.39,0:07:16.33,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Besides, we're almost at his place. \NWe have to keep going!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.26,0:07:22.70,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,*sigh* Alright. \NThere really is no other choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.14,0:07:26.62,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Khan, let's pick up the pace. \NLet me know if you need to switch off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.42,0:07:34.74,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I'm fine for now, little friend. \NLet's move!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.46,0:07:36.26,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.67,0:07:43.57,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Hey, stop treating me like a kid! \NWe aren't that far apart in age, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.24,0:07:47.20,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Haha, see? \NYou really do get mad easily!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.72,0:07:53.84,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Don't tease her! \NBechamel is just terribly worried about Welsh, that's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.52,0:08:00.08,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Oh, miss honest here! \NIt's plain as day that you're head over heels for the cook prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.40,0:08:03.05,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Ooh, hot hot! \NWhoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.11,0:08:15.25,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Oh my, and you're an athlete? \NWhere's your sense of balance? \NYou must be a terrible Gobbowl player!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.75,0:08:17.75,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Ehehe, hahaha!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.67,0:08:23.57,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Girls, I'm glad you found a friend \Nwho gets your sense of humor!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.30,0:08:27.90,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Hahaha, truly!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.06,0:08:31.86,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Dad, I really like this kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.57,0:08:57.37,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,We've arrived!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.97,0:09:03.96,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Only Old Man Kryston, the healer, \Ncan treat His Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.73,0:09:09.36,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Thank goodness! \NHang in there, Welsh, just a little longer!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.59,0:09:18.89,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,We got here faster than I expected. \NWe might actually make it in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.55,0:09:20.61,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be so sure...Joris
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.74,0:09:33.80,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I've heard all about you. Mother searched for you for years, \Nthough recently she stopped caring.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.34,0:09:35.00,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Shedar...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.50,0:09:37.80,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Prince Shedar, you insolent fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.69,0:09:40.24,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,How is he doing? 
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.70,0:09:44.35,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,That impudent brat who defied Mother... \Nis he dead yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.09,0:09:50.11,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,He didn't defy anyone! \NHe's just a cook!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.17,0:09:58.19,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,The dragon spoke of it: a boy from Breshka \Nwith bright blue eyes would stand against Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.43,0:10:01.76,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Dragon? Which dragon are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.35,0:10:07.28,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,If you want to know so badly, \NI'll tell you: the white dragon, Dardondakal.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.71,0:10:15.09,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,That's impossible! Dardondakal was bound to Canel! \NWhy would he betray Canel's son?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.59,0:10:22.09,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Dragons follow logic beyond human understanding. \NSomeone of your stature should know that well enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.79,0:10:27.13,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Shedar, you need to know: \NWelsh is your...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.20,0:10:31.45,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Welsh? \NIs that the name of the traitor who opposes Mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.18,0:10:37.95,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Or is he just a convenient puppet? \NI won't be fooled, Joris!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.05,0:10:42.75,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Hiding in the shadows, pulling the strings... \N{\b1}You{\b0} are the true schemer here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.29,0:10:48.31,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Welsh is the son of Canel and Anette! \NHe is the rightful heir to the throne of Bonta!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.69,0:10:50.11,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,The "{\i1}rightful{\i0}" heir?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.25,0:10:57.79,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,So you foolishly hid his existence for 16 long years, \Nwaiting for a chance to eliminate Mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.33,0:11:04.55,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Tell me then, how could someone like {\i1}"that"{\i0} \Nrule a kingdom? He's a mere cook!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.33,0:11:10.88,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Have you lost your mind? \NOr has revenge blinded your judgment?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.73,0:11:16.60,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Queen Jabelle is a tyrant! \NBecause of her, Bonta has become a terrible realm!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.05,0:11:22.34,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Bonta is the greatest kingdom! \NMother made it the most magnificent nation in the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.84,0:11:23.02,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Girls, get ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.87,0:11:32.94,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Khan Karkass! Of course I know who you are. \NThere's a statue of you at the Bonta Gobbowl Stadium!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.11,0:11:36.72,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Khan Karkass, the Gobbowl legend! 
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.50,0:11:42.40,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Long retired and stricken with illness, why reappear now? \NDid someone feed you absurd ideas?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.83,0:11:45.17,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Who does he think he is?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.27,0:11:47.37,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Just a spoiled prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.92,0:11:52.94,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,If an adventure presents itself, \Nhe can't help but jump in. That is his nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.19,0:11:55.90,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Even at the cost of your daughters' lives?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.79,0:12:01.82,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Or is there another motive behind this? \NWell, it doesn't matter anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.51,0:12:06.42,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I hold a Dofus... \NThe Emerald Dofus!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.41,0:12:22.64,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Wait! My daughters have nothing to do with this! \NSpare them!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.97,0:12:27.98,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Karkass, you call this an adventure, \Nbut this is clear treason!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.54,0:12:32.70,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Aligning with Joris, fleeing with this \Nsupposed son of Canel...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.30,0:12:37.74,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,And to think Her Majesty has constantly \Nsacrificed herself for her people!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.74,0:12:51.26,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,How pathetic. Heroes who contributed to Bonta, \Nreduced to treason, ruining their former glory.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.90,0:12:55.01,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Master Joris, you have a plan, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.98,0:13:03.03,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Wait, Shedar! \NListen to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.03,0:13:03.50,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I have nothing to hear from you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.79,0:13:13.33,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,My daughters... \Nyou truly look so much like your mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.97,0:13:30.14,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Falling from this height, \Nno one would survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.25,0:13:31.84,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Indeed. 
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.60,0:13:35.98,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Her Majesty will surely be \Nproud of Your Highness. 
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.64,0:13:37.64,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Rejoice!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.93,0:13:48.35,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Yes, Mother will be pleased... \Nsince I disposed of these fools.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.07,0:13:54.93,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Yet I feel no joy at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.60,0:14:09.84,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Papa!!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.59,0:14:17.61,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,What a piece of meat! \NWhat should I make?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.35,0:14:26.05,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Khan! \NHas your legendary strength waned?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.50,0:14:33.57,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Honestly, I don't have my old strength anymore. \NBut I guarantee my daughters' talent!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.06,0:14:35.31,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Girls! 
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.57,0:14:40.01,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,It's the final match!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.66,0:14:47.58,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,The final match?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.06,0:14:54.26,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,That's right! \NThis is the world championship final! \NGrab the ball!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.70,0:15:00.47,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Bechamel! I'm opening a portal! \NJust like at Khan's house! 
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.03,0:15:05.80,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,It will appear below, take Welsh and \Ndon't let go of his hand!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.86,0:15:08.81,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Got it! \NAs if I'd let go!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.42,0:15:11.22,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Are you ready?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.96,0:15:19.60,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Life or death, \Nit's up to you guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.32,0:15:24.72,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,3! 2! 1!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.24,0:15:31.97,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Hey, Khan! \NThrow at zero! Zero!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.32,0:15:34.69,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,What?! \NThen go ahead first!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.76,0:15:43.84,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,*{\b1}sigh{\b0}* Anyone can make a mistake. \NAlright, girls, we go on zero!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.20,0:15:45.96,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Got it, no problem!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.60,0:15:51.00,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,3! 2! 1! 0!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.99,0:16:26.06,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Khan, watch out! 
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.82,0:16:30.90,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,That looks like it hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.46,0:16:48.58,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Don't worry Dad, \NI'm okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.86,0:16:58.10,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Girls, move away right now! \NA giant boulder is coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.35,0:17:06.02,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Don't interfere, Dad! \NWe have to save the Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.39,0:17:11.22,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Let's do this together! \NJust like in training!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.67,0:17:20.80,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Girls!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.19,0:17:44.94,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Girls... that was an amazing tackle!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.31,0:17:49.70,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I'd love to showcase that in our next match! \NThe fans will be thrilled!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.19,0:17:54.42,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,A six-armed tackle! \NDad, have you ever seen anything like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.99,0:17:57.72,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,No, it's a first for me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.59,0:18:05.40,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Thank you, everyone! \NAs expected of Gobbowl players! Bravo!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.19,0:18:10.44,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,If your mother were watching, \Nshe'd be so proud of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.30,0:18:20.26,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Thank you, my little friend. \NAre you alright?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.31,0:18:27.38,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,A bit dizzy, but that's common in matches. \NI'll be fine in a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.31,0:18:32.34,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Joris, where have you brought us?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.22,0:18:38.01,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,To my home. As Shedar said, \NI've been hiding for 16 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.10,0:18:43.97,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I only left home to gather intel in Bonta \Nor to visit your house.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.62,0:18:50.90,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Oh my, well, well, well! \NIf it isn't Jojo and the heavy drinker Khan Karkass!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.42,0:18:54.03,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,We're back, Luis. Hey, Luis.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.49,0:18:56.91,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Just so you know, \NI didn't come here to see you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.85,0:19:03.79,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Girls, let me introduce Luis. \NHe's... a demon, so to speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.25,0:19:09.38,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Naturally wicked, \Nbut he decided he wanted to become gentle.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.57,0:19:15.66,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Wow, best introduction ever! \NAfter all the things we've been through together...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.20,0:19:19.98,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Wait, so you've never told your daughters about me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.80,0:19:26.00,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,That's right. I didn't want to give them nightmares. 
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.60,0:19:29.30,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Luis, lower the lift. \NWe're in a rush.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.93,0:19:30.90,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,The Prince is sick.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.30,0:19:34.45,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Sick? \NYou mean he's about to die?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.60,0:19:37.25,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Hey! \NDon't say such ominous things!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.66,0:19:45.90,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the Luis Express, everyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.50,0:19:50.55,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Girls, don't be afraid. 
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.35,0:19:53.67,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Are you saying that from the bottom of your heart, Jojo?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.54,0:20:09.50,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Is my wife around? 
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.70,0:20:11.15,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,She's in the kitchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.65,0:20:25.40,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Lilotte! 
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.00,0:20:28.36,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Stop it, Lilotte! 
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.02,0:20:34.80,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Stop! You didn't contact me for ten days! \NDo you know how worried I was?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.46,0:20:37.75,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I have no intention of stopping, of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.45,0:20:41.40,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Khan! 
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.40,0:20:45.25,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Lilotte, it's been a long time!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.69,0:20:48.39,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Ah, I'm truly so happy to see you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.13,0:20:56.15,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Has your illness not improved? 
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.10,0:21:00.96,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I'm not young anymore, after all! Hahaha!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.63,0:21:07.89,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Oh my, look how big you girls have grown!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.39,0:21:12.39,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Aunt Lilotte, hello!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.51,0:21:16.00,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,I wish you had come to visit me more often!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.00,0:21:20.25,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,My goodness, you girls are injured!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.10,0:21:24.98,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Actually, we need you to look at this boy before us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.95,0:21:37.76,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Is this boy... the Prince?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.30,0:21:47.74,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,Come, let's look at his wounds first. \NThen I'll tend to yours as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.12,0:22:12.73,Welsh and Shedar,,0,0,0,,We resume the pursuit, Shifo.
